From b06826c6e4db9466d18bbef99ea9385ca31e3eca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:48:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] snapshot: recycle copy-on-write nodes through concurrent
 slabs

Use cross-thread slab allocation for immutable mempool entries and radix path copies, and allocate shared snapshot wrappers and template mutex control blocks from the same bounded-chunk allocator policy. Other radix users keep the standard allocator. RCU ownership, immutable reads and copy-on-write behavior are unchanged.

Use 1024-slot chunks to limit incremental retained capacity per size class. Slab refills still call the heap allocator, and dynamic entry metadata and RCU cleanup bookkeeping remain heap-backed. Chunks are retained for process lifetime.

Cover retained snapshot contents through writer removals and reader-thread retirement across multiple slab chunks. Native build, existing suites and source-matched measurements are pending coordinated resources.
